; DOMAIN: k-theory/topological-algebraic [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24]
; Claim: For a compact Hausdorff space X, topological K-theory K^0(X) is the Grothendieck group of the commutative monoid Vect(X) of iso classes of complex vector bundles under direct sum, with tensor product making it a ring; K^0(pt)=Z (rank). Reduced K~^0(X) splits off the rank. Negative groups K^{-n}(X)=K~^0(S^n X+) give a cohomology theory, and Bott periodicity K^{-n}=K^{-n-2} collapses it to two groups K^0,K^1. For a ring R, algebraic K_0(R)=Grothendieck group of finitely-generated projective R-modules, K_1(R)=GL(R)/E(R) (abelianized), higher K_n(R)=pi_n(BGL(R)^+) (Quillen plus construction) or pi_n of the K-theory spectrum. The Chern character ch: K^0(X)⊗Q -> ⊕ H^{2k}(X;Q) is a ring isomorphism rationally.
; Structure: (K^0(X)=Grothendieck(Vect(X),⊕), ring via ⊗) (K^0(pt)=Z) (Bott periodicity K^{-n}=K^{-n-2}, two groups K^0/K^1) (algebraic K_0(R)=Grothendieck(f.g. projective R-modules); K_1(R)=GL(R)/E(R); K_n=pi_n BGL(R)^+) (Chern character K^0⊗Q ≅ ⊕H^{even}(X;Q)).
; Result: K-theory linearizes geometry/algebra by group-completing bundles or projective modules into a generalized cohomology / invariant, with Bott periodicity giving it its characteristic 2-fold structure and the Chern character connecting it rationally to ordinary cohomology.
; Bridge: genesis_homology (K-theory is a generalized cohomology theory satisfying Eilenberg-Steenrod minus dimension; Chern character maps to ordinary H^{even}) + genesis_ext_tor (K_0(R) group-completes projective modules; projectives are the Ext-acyclic objects, tying K-theory to derived-functor homological algebra) + genesis_derived_category (higher K-theory of an exact/triangulated category via Waldhausen S-construction; K-theory of D(A)) + genesis_representation_theory (equivariant K_G^0(pt)=R(G) the representation ring, Grothendieck group of G-reps).
(= (k-theory-zero $X) (grothendieck-group (monoid (vector-bundles $X) direct-sum)))
(= (k-theory-zero point) integers)
(= (bott-periodicity $n) (= (k-theory (negate $n)) (k-theory (negate (plus $n 2)))))
(= (algebraic-k0 $R) (grothendieck-group (fg-projective-modules $R)))
(= (algebraic-k1 $R) (abelianize (quotient (general-linear $R) (elementary-matrices $R))))
(= (chern-character $X) (ring-iso (tensor (k-theory-zero $X) rationals) (even-cohomology $X rationals)))